    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1134">

                <pb facs="1224" n="1212" xml:id="pg1212"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">841.79658/79: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-03-15T13:00:00-04:00">March 15, 1944—1
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1940. Please telegraph whether decision referred to in your 1921, March 9, has
                    yet been made. Norwegian Ambassador informed us that last week King Haakon
                    accompanied by his Prime Minister<anchor n="32" xml:id="d1134-f1"/> and Foreign
                    Minister discussed the matter jointly with Mr. Churchill<anchor n="33"
                        xml:id="d1134-f2"/> and Mr. Eden.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1134-f1" n="32" xml:id="d1134-f1-content">
                <p>Johan Nygaardsvold, Norwegian Prime Minister.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1134-f2" n="33" xml:id="d1134-f2-content">
                <p>Winston S. Churchill, British Prime Minister.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
